<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Anomalocaris canadensis Turing wavenumber k_c at 24 µm (508 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 88.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 accepts the Du sweep (lambda_c from 5.93 to 10.73 cells, monotonic), the equal-diffusion ablation (std ratio about 0.0026), the Tyrrell-cast segmentation (foreground 0.589, circularity 0.303, coherency 0.559), and the stencil-versus-numerical growth-rate fit (Pearson r = 0.999989, RMSE = 0.00626, KS D = 0.071 against a zero-growth null of 0.714). The 508 Ma wavelength remains 2.397e-05 m, below the reconstructed 266 µm Emu Bay facet spacing. What changes at the Ordovician successor is body size, not this cellular wavenumber. Overall 88.3/100 (faithfulness 87.8, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 63ace896bba72dd95b1823861b5b9936be9cf066; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/anomalocaris_canadensis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 63ace896bba72dd95b1823861b5b9936be9cf066, image/png, 661168 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 8c788c0b684071e171d8a48b94401bc5386b600a5228f9624b970e75fdc1be4f (sha256 8c788c0b684071e171d8a48b94401bc5386b600a5228f9624b970e75fdc1be4f), spec_fingerprint 6e60ae9de13486d021af674ae24c3fe415cc4c359fddd14174f41704efc81a34. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6e60ae9de13486d021af674ae24c3fe415cc4c359fddd14174f41704efc81a34; artifact_sha256: 8c788c0b684071e171d8a48b94401bc5386b600a5228f9624b970e75fdc1be4f. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator. | Paterson et al. 2011: 2-3 cm eyes, at least 16000 lenses, Emu Bay Shale, about 515 Ma. | Daley and Edgecombe 2014: stalked eyes on Burgess Shale A. canadensis. | Van Roy and Briggs 2011: Fezouata bodies larger than any Cambrian anomalocaridid, 488-472 Ma.; reconstructed_in_script: k_c^2 = (Dv f_u + Du g_v) / (2 Du Dv) with f_u = 0.8 and g_v = -1, pinned so lambda_c = 2.397e-05 m. | Facet spacing reconstructed from the published diameter and lens count, not measured on a lens row. | Cast segmentation: border-contrast mask, circularity, structure-tensor coherency.; transfer_boundary: The 24 µm mode is a model scale inside a facet. The Tyrrell photograph is a cast about 20 cm long and does not resolve that mode. | Schnakenberg a and b are a spot-capable regime, not a fitted anomalocaridid rate.; does_not_claim: That Burgess Shale pigment chemistry followed these rate constants. | That the Drosophila switch-and-template R8 circuit (Lubensky et al. 2011) operated in A. canadensis. | A second chronospecies of A. canadensis. The series index is 1/1; Emu Bay and Fezouata are lineage brackets.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R5 (open): only one photographed object, and it is a museum cast rather than the original Burgess surface. A second specimen would test whether the mask statistics are about this mount.",
        "remediation needed: R6 (open): a and b are a spot-capable regime, not rates measured on anomalocaridid cuticle. No 24 µm pigment map exists to fit them to.",
        "remediation needed: R7 (open): single assessor. A second provider has not scored this audit." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.83e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Anomalocaris canadensis Turing wavenumber k_c at 24 µm (508 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Scaling both diffusivities from 0.55 to 1.80 moves analytical lambda_c monotonically from 5.93 to 10.73 cells, and every scale stays Turing-unstable. Setting Du = Dv makes the discriminant negative and the field std collapses (ratio about 0.0026)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
