    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Anomalocaris canadensis Turing wavenumber k_c at 24 µm (508 Ma) (Anomalocaris canadensis)",
        "Anomalocaris canadensis Turing wavenumber k_c at 24 µm (508 Ma) faithfully reproduces Anomalocaris canadensis morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0.py, docs/media/anomalocaris_canadensis_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Anomalocaris canadensis specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/anomalocaris_canadensis_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Anomalocaris canadensis" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A second chronospecies of A. canadensis. The series index is 1/1; Emu Bay and Fezouata are lineage brackets.",
        "does_not_claim: That Burgess Shale pigment chemistry followed these rate constants.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Drosophila switch-and-template R8 circuit (Lubensky et al. 2011) operated in A. canadensis.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Cast segmentation: border-contrast mask, circularity, structure-tensor coherency.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Facet spacing reconstructed from the published diameter and lens count, not measured on a lens row.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: k_c^2 = (Dv f_u + Du g_v) / (2 Du Dv) with f_u = 0.8 and g_v = -1, pinned so lambda_c = 2.397e-05 m.",
        "reported_in_source: Daley and Edgecombe 2014: stalked eyes on Burgess Shale A. canadensis.",
        "reported_in_source: Paterson et al. 2011: 2-3 cm eyes, at least 16000 lenses, Emu Bay Shale, about 515 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator.",
        "reported_in_source: Van Roy and Briggs 2011: Fezouata bodies larger than any Cambrian anomalocaridid, 488-472 Ma.",
        "transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg a and b are a spot-capable regime, not a fitted anomalocaridid rate.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 24 µm mode is a model scale inside a facet. The Tyrrell photograph is a cast about 20 cm long and does not resolve that mode." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Anomalocaris canadensis (Middle Cambrian (Burgess Shale, 508 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Anomalocaris" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/anomalocaris_canadensis_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif; output: docs/media/anomalocaris_canadensis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Anomalocaris canadensis; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator. | Paterson et al. 2011: 2-3 cm eyes, at least 16000 lenses, Emu Bay Shale, about 515 Ma. | Daley and Edgecombe 2014: stalked eyes on Burgess Shale A. canadensis. | Van Roy and Briggs 2011: Fezouata bodies larger than any Cambrian anomalocaridid, 488-472 Ma.; reconstructed_in_script: k_c^2 = (Dv f_u + Du g_v) / (2 Du Dv) with f_u = 0.8 and g_v = -1, pinned so lambda_c = 2.397e-05 m. | Facet spacing reconstructed from the published diameter and lens count, not measured on a lens row. | Cast segmentation: border-contrast mask, circularity, structure-tensor coherency.; transfer_boundary: The 24 µm mode is a model scale inside a facet. The Tyrrell photograph is a cast about 20 cm long and does not resolve that mode. | Schnakenberg a and b are a spot-capable regime, not a fitted anomalocaridid rate.; does_not_claim: That Burgess Shale pigment chemistry followed these rate constants. | That the Drosophila switch-and-template R8 circuit (Lubensky et al. 2011) operated in A. canadensis. | A second chronospecies of A. canadensis. The series index is 1/1; Emu Bay and Fezouata are lineage brackets.]; phenomenon_size: 24 µm (2.352e-05 m, log10=-4.629 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 24 µm to 5.3 cm): 24 µm:anomalocaris-canadensis-bioelectric-polarity, 74 µm:anomalocaris-canadensis-vertex-packing, 1.2 mm:anomalocaris-canadensis-turing-wavelength, 2.4 mm:anomalocaris-canadensis-clock-wavefront, 5.3 mm:anomalocaris-canadensis-morphogen-condensation, 6.5 mm:anomalocaris-canadensis-elastic-buckling, 7.3 mm:anomalocaris-canadensis-flux-canalization, 1.0 cm:anomalocaris-canadensis-branching-tree" ;
